invariant: INV-36
file: build.zig
catches: test/zig-build-check.sh
reason: build.zig stops adding the evex512 feature to an x86-64 host
  object's target. Zig then turns evex512 off for every CPU without
  AVX-512, x86-64's baseline and znver3 among them, and clang refuses each
  512-bit argument and return value in rsa_ifma.c, so the object does not
  build for those CPUs. The script's cross row builds colibri's HTTP/2
  object for x86_64-linux-gnu at -Dcpu=baseline on any machine.

--- old
    const target = withEvex512(b, config, b.standardTargetOptions(.{}));
--- new
    const target = b.standardTargetOptions(.{});
